meta {
  name: Update User
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/user
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "Jane D. Updated",
    "email": "jane.new@example.com"
  }
}

docs {
  Updates the authenticated user's profile. Both fields are optional but
  can't be blank when sent (`name` max 255, `email` max 255 and unique
  among both current and pending addresses).

  `email` is **staged, not applied**: the account keeps its current
  address and `pending_email` is set, while a confirmation link goes to
  the new address and a security alert goes to the old one. The change
  only lands when that link is followed (see `Auth/Confirm Email
  Change`), and doing so revokes every session.

  Cancel a staged change with `Cancel Email Change`.

  Response is wrapped: `{ success, statusCode, message, data: { user } }`.
}
